Criteria for Imposing Penalty Surcharges (Related to Article 32)

■ Enforcement Decree of the Act on Carbon Dioxide Capture, Transport, Storage and Utilization [Attached Table 2]

Criteria for Imposing Penalty Surcharges (Related to Article 32)

1. General criteria

  (a) One month of suspension of business under Article 23 (1) of the Act is calculated as 30 days.

  (b) The amount of a penalty surcharge for each type of violation is calculated by multiplying the period of suspension of business by the amount per day of suspension according to the scale of carbon dioxide storage under item 2.

  (c) The period of suspension of business under item (b) means the period calculated under Article 23 (2) of the Act (or the period as increased or reduced, if adjusted).

  (d) Notwithstanding item (b), if the calculated penalty surcharge exceeds 30 million won, the amount of the penalty surcharge shall be 30 million won.

2. Penalty surcharge criteria

| Grade | Scale of carbon dioxide storage | Penalty surcharge per day of suspension (unit: 10,000 won) |
|---|---|---:|
| 1 | Not exceeding 500,000 tons | 5 |
| 2 | More than 500,000 but not exceeding 1,000,000 tons | 8 |
| 3 | More than 1,000,000 but not exceeding 3,000,000 tons | 10 |
| 4 | More than 3,000,000 but not exceeding 5,000,000 tons | 13 |
| 5 | More than 5,000,000 tons | 16 |

Criteria for Imposing Administrative Fines (Related to Article 72)

■ Enforcement Decree of the Act on Carbon Dioxide Capture, Transport, Storage and Utilization [Attached Table 3]

Criteria for Imposing Administrative Fines (Related to Article 72)

1. General criteria

  (a) The increased fine criteria based on the number of violations apply if an administrative fine was imposed for the same violation within the most recent year. The period is calculated from the date on which the administrative fine was imposed for the violation and the date on which a repeat of the same violation was detected after that disposition.

  (b) When an increased fine is imposed under item (a), the applicable violation count shall be the count following that of the disposition imposed before the violation (if there were at least two fines within the period under item (a), the higher count applies).

  (c) The imposing authority may reduce the fine under the individual criteria in item 2 by up to one half in any of the following cases; provided that this does not apply to a violator who is in arrears on an administrative fine:
    1) The violation is deemed to have resulted from minor negligence or error;
    2) The violator is deemed to have made efforts to correct or eliminate the unlawful condition;
    3) A reduction is deemed necessary in light of the degree, motive and consequences of the violation or other circumstances.

  (d) The imposing authority may increase the fine under the individual criteria in item 2 by up to one half in any of the following cases; provided that the increased fine shall not exceed the upper limit under Article 54 (1) and (2) of the Act:
    1) The content and severity of the violation are deemed significant and the resulting harm to the public is substantial;
    2) The unlawful condition has continued for at least six months;
    3) An increase is deemed necessary in light of the degree, motive and consequences of the violation or other circumstances.

2. Individual criteria (unit: 10,000 won)

| Violation | Legal basis | First violation | Second violation | Third or subsequent violation |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| (a) Refusing, obstructing or evading an inspection of compliance with safety management rules under Article 9 (3) of the Act | Article 54 (2) 1 of the Act | 300 | 400 | 500 |
| (b) Failing to report appointment of a safety manager under Article 10 (1) of the Act or making a false report | Article 54 (2) 2 of the Act | 300 | 400 | 500 |
| (c) Failing to report succession to the status of a storage business operator under Article 20 (1) through (3) of the Act or making a false report | Article 54 (2) 3 of the Act | 300 | 400 | 500 |
| (d) Commencing storage business without making a report under the main clause of Article 22 (1) of the Act | Article 54 (1) 1 of the Act | 2,000 | 2,500 | 3,000 |
| (e) Failing to obtain approval of a monitoring plan under Article 25 (1) of the Act | Article 54 (1) 2 of the Act | 1,000 | 1,500 | 2,000 |
| (f) Failing to give notice of leakage in violation of Article 28 (2) of the Act | Article 54 (2) 4 of the Act | 200 | 300 | 400 |
| (g) Placing a certification mark or similar mark on uncertified technology or products in violation of Article 34 (4) of the Act | Article 54 (1) 3 of the Act | 500 | 700 | 1,000 |
| (h) Refusing, obstructing or evading an on-site inspection under Article 47 (1) of the Act | Article 54 (2) 5 of the Act | 100 | 150 | 200 |
